  "contracts": [
    "MUL changes only C from product bit7; EMUL/EMULS use full32-bit NZ and bit15 carry while preserving V and upper flags",
    "Unsigned and signed integer/fractional/extended divides use mathematically expected quotient/remainder and defined flags",
    "Every native divide is guarded against zero divisor before host DIV/IDIV; signed32 EDIVS uses host64 division including int32min/-1",
    "Guest overflow follows documented register retention or quotient saturation and C/V reporting, with all other specified state retained",
    "IDIVS8000/ffff quotient8000/remainder0 are mandatory output checks; only its undefined NZ are checked as explicit policy",
    "Architecturally indeterminate IDIV/FDIV remainders retain D; EDIV/EDIVS error undefined flags retain old bits, separately checked as policy without silicon claim",
    "Generated arithmetic uses no memory/ISA helper or host frame; literal MUL plus ADCA0 consumes the actual carry",
    "Signed16 overflow classification uses one biased unsigned range test, proved for the entire possible quotient interval with two SAT negative controls"
  ],
